# Mirrors .gitignore for the most part; a few entries differ because "not
# tracked by git" and "not needed inside the build context" are different
# questions (ring.json IS tracked and IS needed; node_modules is neither
# tracked nor needed, since the image installs its own).

.git
node_modules
/.svelte-kit
/build

Dockerfile*
docker-compose*.yml
.dockerignore

# Widget bundle, regenerated by `npm run build:widget` during the image
# build itself (see package.json's `build` script, which runs it first).
# Never present in a clean checkout, listed here defensively in case a local
# build artifact is sitting in the working tree when `docker build` runs.
/static/embed.js
/static/embed.v*.js

.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Real secrets never belong in a build context regardless of what the
# Dockerfile does with them; VITE_SUBMISSION_WEBHOOK_URL and friends arrive
# as --build-arg instead (see docs/roadmap.md, .env.example).
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

test-results
/testing/fixtures/
/testing/sites/

# Documentation and CI config are not needed at build or run time.
docs
.github
*.md

# Exception: CHANGELOG.md IS needed at build time. src/routes/+layout.server.js
# imports it with Vite's `?raw` so the About modal's release list is baked
# into the prerendered output rather than fetched at runtime (see that
# file's own doc comment). Omitting this line makes the build fail outright
# with a "file not found" from that import — which is how GGRequestz's
# Dockerfile (the reference this project's own Docker setup was modeled on)
# documents having discovered the same trap; recorded here so it isn't
# rediscovered the same way twice.
!CHANGELOG.md
